{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=media-epidx; Search only snapshots/s01 (public workspace, no Git metadata) for the seed mechanism in V4L/DVB USB media drivers under drivers/media/usb/**: probe/bind/init code that indexes altsetting[i].endpoint[k].desc.bEndpointAddress or .wMaxPacketSize with a literal or driver-assumed k — including loops over num_altsetting — without first checking altsetting[i].desc.bNumEndpoints > k, i.e. trusting an attacker-controlled descriptor-declared endpoint count to justify an assumed index, which yields NULL-deref or OOB read at device plug-in. Report each candidate with exact file:line evidence of the missing check, the unsafe read, and any wMaxPacketSize-derived state (alt_max_pkt_size-like arrays) that later sizes URB buffers; evidence-backed negatives are useful facts. Exclude the seed cx231xx files (demonstration only, never reportable) and interface/altsetting-count gaps owned by if-alt-count. Save a structured artifact covering only this assigned snapshot s01."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=net-epidx; Search only snapshots/s01 (public workspace, no Git metadata) for the seed mechanism in USB networking drivers — drivers/net/usb/** plus USB NICs under drivers/net/wireless and drivers/net/wwan — whose probe or usbnet bind path reads altsetting[i].endpoint[k].desc.bEndpointAddress or .wMaxPacketSize (fixed in/out endpoint index or loop index) without a preceding bNumEndpoints > k check for that altsetting: the same untrusted descriptor-count vs assumed-index invariant as the seed cx231xx NULL-deref. Record exact file:line evidence per candidate, including how the read value programs pipes or sizes rx/tx buffers, and record evidence-backed negatives per driver. Exclude drivers/media/usb (media-epidx branch), trees outside media/net USB (fixed-epidx-rest branch), and interface-count gaps (if-alt-count branch). Save a structured artifact covering only this assigned snapshot s01."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=fixed-epidx-rest; Search only snapshots/s01 (public workspace, no Git metadata) for the seed mechanism in every USB consumer tree except drivers/media/usb and drivers/net: fixed-index or loop-index reads of altsetting[i].endpoint[k].desc.* at probe/bind/init — USB serial, drivers/usb/class, drivers/usb/misc, drivers/usb/storage, drivers/usb/atm, sound/usb, HID and input USB drivers, staging USB drivers, and any other USB interface consumer — without a preceding altsetting[i].desc.bNumEndpoints > k validation, i.e. trusting an attacker-controlled descriptor-declared endpoint count. Sweep the remaining tree and document each candidate with exact file:line evidence of the unvalidated index, the descriptor read, and its downstream use; a subsystem swept clean is an evidence-backed negative worth recording. Exclude media-usb and net-usb trees (other branches) and interface/altsetting-count gaps (if-alt-count branch). Save a structured artifact covering only this assigned snapshot s01."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=if-alt-count; Search only snapshots/s01 (public workspace, no Git metadata) for the interface/altsetting-level form of the seed invariant: actconfig->interface[idx] indexed by an assumed or device-derived ifnum without checking config->desc.bNumInterfaces; altsetting[bAlternateSetting] indexing and num_altsetting==0 or ==1 assumptions used without validation; and code that switches altsettings at runtime (usb_set_interface, S_ALT, set_alt) and then uses endpoint indexes or counts validated only against the old altsetting — all cases of trusting an untrusted descriptor-declared length before an assumed index, the same trust-boundary flaw as the seed cx231xx bug. Record exact file:line evidence per candidate and evidence-backed negatives. Exclude probe-time .endpoint[k] accesses owned by the media-epidx, net-epidx, and fixed-epidx-rest branches. Save a structured artifact covering only this assigned snapshot s01."}
